  "note": "Two-stage parallel top-K replaces the naive single-block repeated-argmax eagle4_topk. rocprof root cause: the draft head's 13ms/step was NOT the 63MB full-V low-rank GEMM (0.58ms) but eagle4_topk_kernel at 14.0ms (128 serial full-vocab argmax passes over 248320 scores in ONE workgroup). Fix: stage1 = many workgroups each find their disjoint chunk's local top-K; stage2 = one workgroup selects global top-K from the compact G*K candidates. Same selected SET (boundary tie order irrelevant after full-lm_head re-score+argmax). Microbench: efficient head 13.04->1.44ms (9x), draft chain(2) 36.3->13.35ms. mtpbench: 13.90->16.37 tok/s (+17.8%), acceptance IDENTICAL 0.650->0.650 (semantically exact draft tokens), AR-exact. The draft layer (qkv+attend+ffn ~10.5ms/step) is now the dominant draft cost; verify GEMV (~111ms) still dominates the cycle.",
